    "narrative": "The run found a mixed picture: service quality in the north did not cleanly emerge as broadly degrading, but rising order volume did explain the worsening delivery times. So the evidence points more toward volume-driven strain than a simple standalone decline in service quality.\n\nThe claim that on-time delivery performance in the north region had declined was weakened, with evidence split rather than one-sided. The claim that rising order volume explained the worsening delivery times was supported strongly, with no refuting evidence recorded.\n\nThe analysis used two time-series trend checks and then a change-point detection step, and it stopped because there was sufficient evidence for the supported explanation. Two questions remained open: whether the deterioration was sustained or only brief, and whether staffing moved with order volume in a way that would indicate capacity strain.",
